# DTF tier manifest: migration-package-catalog  (artifact-keeper#4691 / #4657)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mock-artifactory-catalog. Both
# defects are in the migration importer's registration step, after the bytes
# are stored, so the storage dimension is irrelevant; a migration SOURCE that
# serves real Maven and Debian files is what the tier needs.
#
# THE BUGS
#   #4691 (fixed by #4735). Since #2676 the importer registers migrated
#   artifacts in the package catalog (`packages` / `package_versions`, which
#   the Packages tab and `GET /api/v1/packages?repository_key=` read), but
#   `migration_catalog_entry` returned None for maven/gradle/sbt/ivy: the
#   filename parser recovers only the artifactId while a live `mvn deploy`
#   catalogues `groupId:artifactId`. A Maven repository migrated from Nexus or
#   Artifactory therefore stored every file and listed no packages at all.
#
#   #4657 (fixed by #4741). The importer copied `.deb` files without
#   registering them. `parse_name_and_version` had no Debian parser, so no
#   version and no catalog row; no `debian` control document was written, so
#   `dists/<d>/<c>/binary-<arch>/Packages` was synthesised from the file name
#   and lost every control field ("Description: No description available");
#   and a `.deb` outside `pool/<component>/` (Artifactory's "Set Me Up" path is
#   `pool/<file>.deb`) was stored where the Packages query never looks, so apt
#   could not see it at all.
#
# PRIMITIVES
#   * profiles/upstreams.mock-artifactory-catalog.yml: a stdlib-python mock of
#     the Artifactory API subset `ArtifactoryClient` uses (a copy of the
#     migration-progress-monotonic mock, adapted), reporting packageType
#     `maven` / `debian` so the migration provisions native destinations.
#   * fixtures/build_catalog.py builds the source files on the host at oracle
#     time (a real jar + pom + .sha1/.md5 sidecars + maven-metadata.xml; two
#     real `.deb` ar archives, one pooled, one flat) and the oracle `docker cp`s
#     them into the mock. Timestamps are pinned, so the bytes are identical on
#     both images and every download is compared by sha256.
#
# Oracle gates (discriminating, RELEASE_GATE=1):
#   (CONTROL)  each migration ends `completed` with completed == total == the
#              source file count and 0 failed, into a destination of the right
#              format; the jar downloads byte-identical via /maven/, the pooled
#              `.deb` via /debian/. These hold on BOTH images.
#   (FIX #4691) the Packages-tab API lists exactly `com.dtf:demo 1.0.0` for the
#              migrated Maven repository (sidecars and maven-metadata.xml are
#              not packages), and packages x package_versions holds that row.
#   (FIX #4657) the Packages-tab API lists `dtfpkg 1.0` and `dtfflat 2.0`;
#              the binary-amd64 `Packages` stanza for dtfpkg carries the
#              control file's Description and the file's SHA256; the flat
#              `.deb` is indexed at `pool/main/dtfflat_2.0_all.deb` and
#              downloads from there.
#   (RECOVERY) with the Maven catalog deleted, `reindex-storage` (#1570)
#              registers nothing (CONTROL: it only adds rows for objects that
#              have none, and never touches the catalog) and the #3659 admin
#              backfill restores `com.dtf:demo 1.0.0` (pre-existing, passes on
#              both). With the Debian control documents and catalog deleted
#              (a pre-fix import), RE-RUNNING the migration re-registers both
#              packages, which is #4741's documented recovery (RED on 1.11.1).
#
# NOTE on the pooled .deb on 1.11.1: its Packages stanza is NOT absent there.
# The index falls back to the file name for a `pool/<component>/` row with no
# control document, so the gate keys on the control file's Description and
# not on the package name alone.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle polls job state once a second.
# UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the source sits on a private subnet.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-artifactory-catalog"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
